<p>Saying it like that it looks like a pokemon.</p>
<p>I think more mystery could be added to it. Particulary, the idea of an entity being discovered because of a epidemy looks promising but I don't think its original.</p>
<p>Also, if the parasite is able to make the host produces an eletromagnectic pulse wouldnt the infected people also being able to do that? Basically if each infected is capable of producing a EMP, no eletronics would work in a very big area. It could even be a global threat to take the world back to the dark ages depending on how faster the epidemy spreads. The infected are counscious of that? Or they are emmiting an EMP without knowing? A lot of information is missing.</p>
<p>You have some key elements here that you have to tie together: the creature, the parasite, the epidemy and the eletromagnectic pulse. What is the creature? It has a reason to look like that? If the parasite is able to preserve tissue to survive inside the creature like its alive, it could REALLY be a Prolibytherium. It could make the host emit a EMP because eletricity could be a danger to him, etc, etc.</p>
<p>Have a great day!</p>

