						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13942895/hot-sirens-in-your-area-greenlights-needed">HOT SIRENS IN YOUR AREA - Greenlights needed!</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846598">
									

<p>I actually like this one. You've taken an old critter and had some fun with it. It would be interesting to see the ads be a sort of cognitohazard, in that once someone sees an ad they are compelled to answer the ad and follow through on it.</p>
<p>This would force The Foundation to make a D-Class follow the ad, and then an MTF follow the D-Class to the sirens. Of course, this could create an interesting chase as the sirens see the MTF coming from a mile away. The Foundation would then administer some sort of anti-memetic to relieve the stress in the D-Class, who is unable to complete his quest.</p>
<p>Of course, the MTF could lose the D-Class, and when they followed the tracker find the corpse of the D-Class, forcing them to repeat the process until they find the sirens.</p>
<p>While I'm not sure you really need paratech here (the sirens' intent should be enough), another option would be to have the sirens run a newspaper and run the ads themselves. That not only gives them greater control over the ads, but also gives them a better lead time if someone starts investigating the ads.</p>
<p>You've got a great idea; I hope it works out!</p>

							</div>

								
					
